Description: Support libarchive-based unrar-free as a checked RAR fallback
 Add a separate adapter for unrar-free >= 0.3.0, preserving member names and
 sizes and checking stdout lengths and process status before publishing files.
 Use sequential batches for solid RAR5; suppress directory creation by print.
 Prefer 7z only if RAR3/RAR5 decoders are present, since Debian's free 7z can
 list RAR archives without being able to decompress their members. Preserve
 RARLabs and fully capable 7z priority, and remove unrar-free startup warnings.
 Include real RAR regression fixtures from libarchive 3.7.4, with its license.
Author: Jannik Winkel <jannik.winkel@kiney.de>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-02
